{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Eleven days from Horeb.</b> This too is among the rebukes. He says: from Horeb to Kadesh Barnea is eleven days, and you traversed them in three days. From this you may understand that your sins caused you to linger in the wilderness forty years, for had it not been so, the journey would have been shortened for you, but through your sins it was lengthened. And how did they traverse it in three days? We find that on the twentieth of Iyyar they departed from Horeb, as it is said (Numbers 10:11): ״ויהי בשנה השנית בחדש השני בעשרים בחדש נעלה הענן״, and on the twenty-ninth of Sivan they sent spies from Kadesh Barnea. And if you count backward from the twenty-ninth of Sivan to the twentieth of Iyyar — thirty days — they spent six of those days at Kivrot HaTa'avah in the eating of the meat, and seven days in Hazerot for Miriam's quarantine; it turns out that in three days they traveled the entire way." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> Eileh HaDevarim Rabbah — ״אחד עשר יום מחורב״: eleven days were Israel whole with the Holy One, blessed be He — that is, of the forty days that Moses was on the mountain, Israel was whole with Him for only eleven days and no more; for twenty-nine days, to complete the forty, they were plotting to make the calf. And one said: two days they were whole at Horeb, no more, as it is said (Isaiah 28): ״ואותי יום יום ידרושון״. And one said: one day, as it is said (Deuteronomy 4:10): ״יום אשר עמדת לפני ה' אלהיך בחורב״. And one said: not even one day were they whole — on that very day they committed idolatry, as it is said (Isaiah 17:11): ״ביום נטעך תשגשגי״. Another interpretation: ״אחד עשר יום מחורב״ — by means of one of the Ten Commandments you provoked Him, from Horeb."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The final phrase 'מחורב' is read by the Midrash as 'from Horeb' in the plain sense but also as a pun on חורבה (destruction), or possibly 'by one (אחד) of the ten (עשר)' — the Midrash rereads the words אחד עשר as 'one of the ten.' Rendered hyper-literally to preserve the wordplay."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:35.969732188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}